 Helm with Prometheus Monitoring
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure Prometheus to monitor Kubernetes clusters and Helm releases
Deploy Grafana for visualization of monitoring data
Set up monitoring dashboards to track Helm deployment metrics
Configure service discovery for automatic monitoring of Helm-deployed applications
Create custom alerts for Helm release health monitoring
Understand the integration between Helm, Prometheus, and Grafana for comprehensive monitoring
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Familiarity with Helm package manager fundamentals
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Basic Linux command-line experience
Understanding of monitoring concepts and metrics
